            {
              "id": "e2dd4203-5d5b-4c08-b9bb-bc5b99c2bf6a",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Meditations on the Tarot</strong></em> was originally written by Valtentin Tomberg in French May 21, 1967, but only later published posthumously &amp; anonymously in 1980."
            },
            {
              "id": "df165178-64e4-4697-889e-ff40a05dd01d",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "ab857d14-3e3d-4f12-a169-ebb8acb27208",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Written anonymously and published posthumously, as was the author’s wish, the intention of this work is for the reader to find a relationship with the author in the spiritual dimensions of existence. The author wanted not to be thought of as a personality who lived from 1900 to 1973, but as a friend who is communicating with us from beyond the </em><a href=\"#/magic-circle\"><em>boundaries</em></a><em> of ordinary life.<br><br>Using the 22 major arcana of the </em><a href=\"#/tarot\"><em>tarot</em></a><em> deck as a means to explore some of humanity’s most penetrating spiritual questions, </em>Meditations on the Tarot<em> has attracted an unprecedented range of praise from across the spiritual spectrum.</em>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
